<title>BELGIUM: EU says clears BBC deal.</title>
<headline>EU says clears BBC deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had cleared the acquisition of joint control of the British company HSCo, which comprises the business of the home service transmission of BBC.</p>
<p>&quot;This joint control will be exercised by Castle Tower Communications and Berkshire Fund IV LP of the United States, Telediffusion de France International SA and Candover Plc of the UK,&quot; the Commission said in a statement. </p>
<p>The joint venture will principally provide terrestrial transmission services in Britain, the Isle of Man and the Channel Islands.</p>
<p>The Commission said the acquisition did not give rise to any addition of market shares and that it did not create or strengthen a dominant position.</p>
<p>Telediffusion de France International SA is controlled by France Telecom. Candover Investments and Berkshire Fund IV LP are both investment firms.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
